    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0325" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg237"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Squiers to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-02-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 12, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 853.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm on the overleaf
                    my telegram to the Department reporting an outrage committed against the United
                    States consulate at Cienfuegos, and to inclose copies of correspondence had with
                    the foreign office.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Everybody, from the President down to the lowest official concerned, has been
                    most profuse in apologies and regrets.</p>
                <p>Mr. Palma, as a result of my protests, immediately sent General Rodriguez to
                    Cienfuegos to inquire into the situation and, if he found it necessary, to
                    provide for a stronger force of rural guards.</p>
                <p>I also sent Captain Hanna tc look over the situation, to the end that you might
                    be as closely informed as possible.</p>
                <p>* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d201-a1.xml" xpointer="d201-a1"/>
